{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The step drill bit feels like a useful next tool because enlarging sheet-metal holes complements my cobalt drill set and rivet tools.",
    "The 1/4-20 flat-head screws and M8 bolts connect to sizes in my rivet-nut kits; the M8 bolts could also fill a gap beyond my recent M4–M6 assortment.",
    "The self-drilling screws and duct tape fit the practical fastening and repair work reflected in my purchases."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The M3 and M6 screw packs overlap with assortments I recently bought, without giving me a clear reason to need more of those exact sizes.",
    "The #14 screws and three-inch machine screws feel too specific without a matching task; a familiar thread alone does not make the length useful.",
    "The truss-head screws are relevant, but I would choose the flat-head pack now rather than buy both head styles in the same thread and length."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My repeated hardware purchases seem to be taken as a reason to keep buying individual screw packs, even when I may already have suitable stock.",
    "Matching a thread size from my rivet-nut assortment seems to count too heavily without enough attention to length, head shape, and intended use."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My recent assortments matter because they may already cover a recommended size; I am more interested when an item fills a plausible gap.",
    "Tools that add a capability, such as enlarging holes for fastening work, can be more useful to me now than additional quantities of familiar hardware.",
    "Several items can fit my interests while still being alternatives to one another rather than things I would buy together."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations understand my repair and assembly interests, but sometimes confuse related hardware with a useful next purchase."
}"}
